      "Turn-flow example: 1. Setup: Each player receives chips (e.g. 3 each). Deal 3 cards each plus dealer's extra hand; dealer's rejected 3 form the table pool.\n2. Play: Player to dealer's left acts first; turn passes clockwise. On your turn you may: (a) exchange one card with one table card, (b) exchange all three hand cards for the three table cards, or (c) pass. You may not exchange exactly two cards.\n3. Special combinations: Feuer (three aces = 32) or Schnauz (31 in one suit) must be exposed immediately and the hand ends.\n4. If all pass in succession, replace the three table cards with three from the talon and continue.\n5. A player may close at end of turn; then each other player gets one more turn and the hand ends.\n6. Scoring: Expose hands. Score = sum of one suit (or three of a kind: 30.5, except three aces = 32). Worst hand loses one chip. Feuer: all except holder lose a chip. Last chip lost = swimming; one more loss and you drop out. Last survivor wins.",
